    it would be beyond our responsibility (as a pure-perl module)
    to re-implement this overflow guard in pre-5.8.0 perls, so...
    just skip them and tell people to use bigint then lol XD

    this also means the silly +1 +2 +3 tests are practically
    useless, since the precision is lost anyways and they'd
    be all equal purely by round-off errors. :( ironically
    the only one that caught the round-off error was an exact
    value such as -1 in this case... (and ivmin is only correct
    because -2^(64) is a multiple of 2^(64 - 53).)

